1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,828
The consequences arrived slowly, the way a fox creeps along a hedge.

2
00:00:04,828 --> 00:00:13,066
The union had accepted the report, but the registration office wanted a printed copy without changes.

3
00:00:13,066 --> 00:00:17,616
“Every edit must be approved,” a young clerk said.

4
00:00:17,616 --> 00:00:29,760
“From now on, the map is a document, not a notion.” His phone rang twice while he was speaking, and he did not answer it.

5
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,669
Several volunteers left.

6
00:00:32,669 --> 00:00:43,878
The doubt in the canteen was easy to hear: some said the project had become official, many said it had become useless, and a few said both.

7
00:00:43,878 --> 00:00:58,436
“An opinion is not evidence,” Maya said, “but every opinion is a signal.” She kept a bag of cards with the various complaints written on them, one card for each gate.

8
00:00:58,436 --> 00:01:03,536
Lin went home for a weekend and helped his uncle on the plantation.

9
00:01:03,536 --> 00:01:11,050
They planted cabbage and paddy, checked a grape vine, and watched a bud open into bloom.

10
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:16,169
“A crop fails for a hundred reasons,” his uncle said.

11
00:01:16,169 --> 00:01:31,297
“A wise farmer saves the seed and keeps the sheep away from the beans.” It was the opposite of a rocket launch: no single event, only survival, and at least a million small decisions.

12
00:01:31,297 --> 00:01:36,366
The test he needed was simpler than any assurance from the university.

13
00:01:36,366 --> 00:01:43,790
He stood on the grass beside the canteen and watched a boy and a lady with a cane take the route he had drawn.

14
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:46,585
The impression was not good.

15
00:01:46,585 --> 00:01:54,484
The frame of the sign had been broken by the stem of a fallen tree, and the lead paint on the post had peeled.

16
00:01:54,484 --> 00:02:00,243
His eye followed the damage and his usually steady mood slipped.

17
00:02:00,243 --> 00:02:04,358
Most of the team still wanted to preserve the map.

18
00:02:04,358 --> 00:02:09,332
They could not do it without money, and the money was uncertain.

19
00:02:09,332 --> 00:02:23,946
“Every plan needs a moon to aim at,” Lin wrote, “and a canteen to meet in.” The produce of that winter was small: one page, per gate, signed by the self that wrote it.

20
00:02:23,946 --> 00:02:29,160
He did not know why the sentence pleased him, but he kept it.

21
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:35,803
Enough people cared; quite a few of them were sitting in that room.
